      ":question/worked-solution": "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2 x^{2} - 4}{y^{2} + 2} \\\\ (y^{2} + 2)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 x^{2} - 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (y^{2} + 2)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2 x^{2} - 4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2} + 2)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (2 x^{2} - 4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (y^{2} + 2)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2 x^{2} - 4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y^2\\,\\text{d}y+\\int 2\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x^2\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{y^3}{3}+2y & =\\frac{2x^3}{3}-4x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^{3}}{3} + 2 y=\\frac{2 x^{3}}{3} - 4 x+C.\n$$",
